WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.200
So far each GROUP BY query produced one specific
grain Advanced grouping

00:00:05.225 --> 00:00:10.350
features let one query return several summary grains
together GROUPING SETS is

00:00:10.375 --> 00:00:16.412
the most explicit You list exactly which grouping
combinations you want This

00:00:16.425 --> 00:00:19.438
is useful when a report needs selected summary
levels and you do

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:25.888
not want every possible combination ROLLUP is
designed for hierarchical summaries With

00:00:25.912 --> 00:00:30.425
category and product it can produce detail by
category and product subtotals

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:35.400
by category and a grand total That is a natural
hierarchy product

00:00:35.412 --> 00:00:41.262
belongs under category CUBE produces every grouping
combination for the listed dimensions

00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:45.588
With two dimensions it gives detail by both totals
by the first

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:50.212
totals by the second and the overall grand total
These tools reduce

00:00:50.238 --> 00:00:53.200
the need to write several separate GROUP BY queries
and combine them

00:00:53.212 --> 00:00:57.288
with UNION ALL The tradeoff is that the result
contains rows with

00:00:57.312 --> 00:01:02.388
different grains That means we must label subtotal
and grand-total rows carefully

00:01:02.412 --> 00:01:07.100
so users can interpret them correctly In the next
slides pay attention

00:01:07.125 --> 00:01:10.150
not only to the SQL syntax but also to what each
output

00:01:10.175 --> 00:01:11.075
row represents
